_🧹 Nitpick_ | _🔵 Trivial_

**Consider expanding test coverage for accessibility features.**

The PR adds several accessibility improvements (live region announcements, duplicate prevention feedback, maxTags limit feedback), but the tests don't verify these behaviors. Consider adding tests for:

1. **Live region announcements** - Verify the `aria-live` region content updates
2. **Duplicate tag prevention** - Verify behavior when adding an existing tag
3. **Tag removal** - Verify clicking remove button removes the tag
4. **Backspace removal** - Verify backspace removes the last tag when input is empty



<details>
<summary>💡 Example additional tests</summary>

```typescript
it('announces when a tag is added', () => {
  render(<TagInputWrapper initialTags={[]} />);
  const input = screen.getByPlaceholderText('Add a tag');

  fireEvent.change(input, { target: { value: 'react' } });
  fireEvent.keyDown(input, { key: 'Enter', code: 'Enter' });

  expect(screen.getByRole('status')).toHaveTextContent('Tag react added');
});

it('removes a tag when remove button is clicked', () => {
  render(<TagInputWrapper initialTags={['react']} />);
  const removeButton = screen.getByRole('button', { name: 'Remove react' });

  fireEvent.click(removeButton);

  expect(screen.queryByText('react')).not.toBeInTheDocument();
});

it('prevents duplicate tags and announces', () => {
  render(<TagInputWrapper initialTags={['react']} />);
  const input = screen.getByPlaceholderText('Add a tag');

  fireEvent.change(input, { target: { value: 'react' } });
  fireEvent.keyDown(input, { key: 'Enter', code: 'Enter' });

  // Should still only have one 'react' tag
  expect(screen.getAllByText('react')).toHaveLength(1);
});
```

Note: You may need to query the `<output>` element differently (e.g., by `aria-live` attribute or text content) since it may not have an implicit role of "status".
</details>

<details>
<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>

```
In `@apps/web/src/components/ui/tag-input.test.tsx` around lines 11 - 32, Add
tests to cover the accessibility behaviors introduced in TagInput: render
TagInputWrapper and assert the live region (query by role('status') or aria-live
attribute) updates when tags are added/duplicates are attempted (e.g., after
simulating input change + Enter check that the live region contains "Tag X
added" or duplicate feedback); add a test that clicks the remove button found
via getByRole('button', { name: 'Remove <tag>' }) and asserts the tag text is
removed (queryByText returns null); add a test that types Backspace with an
empty input to ensure the last tag is removed (simulate keyDown on the input
with key 'Backspace' and assert the last tag no longer exists); and add a
duplicate-prevention test that attempts to add an existing tag and asserts only
one instance remains (getAllByText length === 1) and the live region announces
the duplicate message.
```

</details>

